<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  iCemDataMonitor MSI — production installer skeleton.

  OWNER LAW (2026-08-24, amended 2026-08-26): "dumb extractor" — this MSI
  ONLY extracts files. PROHIBITED here (do not add later):
    * shortcuts (no Icon/Shortcut/ProgId),
    * Windows services / SCM entries,
    * environment variables,
    * registry keys of our components (no Registry/Run-keys/autostart),
    * HKCU Run-keys, scheduled tasks, autorun tricks.

  2026-08-26 AMENDMENT (owner request): the installer still writes nothing
  itself, but the wizard now OFFERS desktop-shortcut and autostart options
  as opt-in checkboxes (OptionsDlg). A checked box only schedules a
  deferred CA that runs a plain script installed under
  iCemMonitor\scripts\ (host project scripts\ folder). The scripts do the
  work; each is intentionally one trivial action (see header comments in
  the scripts).

  2026-08-28 AMENDMENT (owner request — LLM improvement points #11/#12/#14):
  the checkbox wiring moved from script CAs to NATIVE MSI elements —
  deterministic, transactional, cleanly removed at uninstall:
    * desktop shortcut = <Shortcut> in a DesktopFolder component gated by
      CREATEDESKTOPSHORTCUT=1 (was create-desktop-shortcut.ps1 CA);
    * autostart = <RegistryValue> HKCU Run value iCemDataMonitorHost =
      "<host exe>" + the autostart flag, gated by ADDAUTOSTART=1 (was
      add-autostart.ps1 CA). NOTE: the target is the HOST (not the emulator —
      the emulator is an independent app and never autostarts); the value
      name/shape matches Host\Tray\AutostartManager + the SetAutostart RPC,
      so the WinUI «Автозагрузка host'а» checkbox and the installer toggle
      the SAME key;
    * <Icon> + ARPPRODUCTICON added so the product entry (when not hidden —
      see ARPSYSTEMCOMPONENT below, which stays per the 2026-08-24 owner
      law) carries the real app icon instead of a blank one.
  The scripts stay shipped under iCemMonitor\scripts\ for manual ops use;
  the MSI no longer invokes them.

  ARPSYSTEMCOMPONENT=1 -> the product is NOT listed in "Programs and
  Features"; upgrade/repair UI is suppressed. Owner decision: uninstall ==
  delete folders (C:\ProgramData\Halliburton\iCem\DataMonitoring and the
  Bin\Modules dll under the iCem install dir; runtime-created user data —
  config.ini, logs, Data.dat — survives where it is not MSI-owned).

  2026-08-28 AMENDMENT #2 (owner request — «миграция программы на
  C:\ProgramData\Halliburton\iCem\DataMonitoring»): the monitor payload moves
  OUT of Program Files into the writable data folder that ALREADY hosts
  Data.dat (and, after this build, the program binaries + config.ini —
  «рядом с бинарником»). MONITORROOT is now
  [CommonAppDataFolder]\Halliburton\iCem\DataMonitoring. Consequences:
    * version bumped 1.0.0 -> 1.0.1 AND ProductCode CHANGED (MajorUpgrade can
      only remove a DIFFERENT ProductCode; the 2026-08-27 «stable ProductCode»
      law is preserved WITHIN a version line — same-version reinstalls still
      get Burn Present -> REINSTALL amus). The old 1.0.0 product (Program
      Files) is removed by MajorUpgrade before files are laid down.
    * station.ini is NO LONGER SHIPPED: the host creates/migrates its config
      itself at first run (IniConfig 2026-08-28 law: canonical
      ProgramData\Halliburton\iCem\DataMonitoring\config.ini; legacy
      station.ini loaded + best-effort migrated, never fatal; web_on=1
      by default).
    * no new ACL work needed: the MSI creates only DIRECTORIES here (Users
      inherit create-file rights under ProgramData); every file the host
      writes (config.ini, logs) is created by the RUNNING user -> user-owned
      -> writable. The AddIn keeps feeding Data.dat in the same folder.
    * [MONITORROOT]-formatted values (desktop shortcut target, autostart Run
      value) resolve to the new path automatically.

  2026-09-01 PM AUTOPSY (owner report «баг в установке — в реестре остались
  прошлые версии») — the stable-ProductCode-within-version law is REPEALED;
  ProductCode="*" (auto per build) is the law now. Two live failures forced it:
    * Error 1731 (repair/reconfigure «source package out of sync»): a rebuilt
      MSI keeps the ProductCode but gets a NEW PackageCode (unavoidable — the
      package changed), so Windows Installer maintenance from the rebuilt
      source refuses: the cached client package ≠ the clicked file. Every
      same-version rebuild was a repair-bomb on installed machines.
    * Error 10005 («A newer version is already installed»): the owner clicked
      an OLDER dist MSI over the installed newer one; MajorUpgrade blocked the
      downgrade by design.
  With ProductCode="*" every build is a NEW product and MajorUpgrade
  (AllowSameVersionUpgrades=yes + AllowDowngrades=yes, UpgradeCode stable
  forever) removes whatever was there — ANY clicked MSI installs cleanly, in
  either version direction, and the old product's uninstall runs with
  UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE so config.ini/Data.dat survive. The Burn-era
  XamlParseException rationale below (mixed old dlls + new xbf/pri) is moot:
  RemoveExistingProducts (afterInstallValidate) deletes the old payload BEFORE
  files are laid down, so no mixed-version folder can occur.

  HISTORICAL (superseded): ProductCode was stable within a version
  (2026-08-27…2026-09-01 AM) to make Burn treat rebuilds as Present and run
  REINSTALLMODE=amus over them; Burn was retired 2026-08-31, and the scheme
  died on the 1731/10005 autopsy above. Version history: 1.4.3
  {EB19620A-01E8-4B3D-8122-C12CC57B6CE6} · 1.4.4
  {925CBE5D-2387-4740-A330-15353F40DDD8} · 1.4.5
  {764BDC6F-FA4E-4F76-8FD3-2CBF222F9E8B} (last hand-rotated code; payload:
  config.ini default lansniffer_on=1 + H.NotifyIcon tray + trimmed host +
  package train 10.0.0).

  REINSTALLMODE=amus -> 'a' = reinstall ALL files regardless of versions or
  missing status; 'm' = rewrite machine hives; 'u' = reinstall all
  user-registry entries; 's' = reinstall shortcuts. This is the extractor
  semantics: every install-over-install rewrites the full payload.

  UAC is ON at the stand, so Scope="perMachine" (since 2026-08-28 AMENDMENT
  #2 the monitor payload lives under CommonAppDataFolder; ICEMDIR for the
  AddIn is still under Program Files).

  2026-08-31 AMENDMENT (owner decree «делаем self-contained!»): the host
  and cli now publish SELF-CONTAINED single-file — the .NET 10 runtime is
  INSIDE the payload, the target machine needs nothing preinstalled. The
  Burn bootstrapper (Bundle.wxs, the runtime chain, the RegistrySearch
  detection) is RETIRED and archived to installer\_archive\burn\: its last
  standing bug (searches authored inside a <Fragment> are silently dropped
  by the linker, so the runtime status line could never go green) died
  with the layer. THIS MSI IS THE ONLY INSTALLER ARTIFACT — end users run
  the .msi directly (optionally via the handoff zip). History: BUG 1722
  (2026-08-26) had pushed runtime install OUT of this MSI into Burn
  (deferred runtime bundles deadlock on the _MSIExecute mutex); with
  self-contained there is no runtime install at all.

  util:CloseApplication x4: the extractor must never fail with "file in use".
  CloseMessage sends WM_CLOSE first, TerminateProcess=1 is the fallback,
  RebootPrompt=no (never force a reboot). iCem.exe (the main Halliburton
  app) is NOT in this list — it is closed ONLY by an explicit user choice
  on the conflict gate (IcemRunningCheckDlg "Закрыть всё" -> WMI Terminate,
  owner decision 2026-08-26); the gate detects a running iCem plus any
  already-installed monitor processes and offers "Закрыть всё" (installer
  kills them) or "Обновить" (re-check after the operator closed them
  manually).

  ICEMDIR resolution: default C:\Program Files\Halliburton\iCem; the
  DirectorySearch (Depth=0, AppSearch) detects the existing iCem install
  folder; if not found the WixUI_InstallDir dialog asks the user and the
  answer is bound to the ICEMDIR property. The AddIn dll is installed into
  [ICEMDIR]\Bin\Modules\Burservis.iCem.DataMonitor.dll.

  UpgradeCode {34A0FD7C-EBD5-4E28-BA96-AE6575896F32} is STABLE across all
  versions — MajorUpgrade (Schedule=afterInstallValidate) removes whatever is
  installed (older, same, or NEWER — 2026-09-01 PM: downgrades ALLOWED, the
  owner clicks any dist MSI and it must just install) before files are laid
  down.

  Build-time defines:
    MsiVersion   - product version, e.g. 1.0.0 (maps to WiX x.y.z)
    AssetsDir    - absolute path to installer\assets
  ============================================================================
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs"
     xmlns:util="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs/util"
     xmlns:ui="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs/ui">

  <!-- ARPSYSTEMCOMPONENT=1: hidden from ARP (see owner law above).
       Codepage=1251: the IcemRunningCheckDlg strings are Russian; the stock
       WixUI strings are plain ASCII, so they survive 1251 unchanged. -->
  <Package Name="iCem Data Monitor"
           Manufacturer="Burservis"
           Version="$(var.MsiVersion)"
           UpgradeCode="{34A0FD7C-EBD5-4E28-BA96-AE6575896F32}"
            ProductCode="*"
           Scope="perMachine"
           Compressed="yes"
           InstallerVersion="500"
           Codepage="1251">

    <SummaryInformation Description="iCem Data Monitor — file extraction MSI (host+cli-in-one + shell + emulator + iCem AddIn). Uninstall == delete folders + wipe runtime data." />

    <!-- 2026-09-01 PM (owner report «баг в установке»): AllowDowngrades="yes"
         ALONE — WiX forbids combining it with AllowSameVersionUpgrades
         (WIX0035), and it SUBSUMES it: the Upgrade row loses the upper
         VersionMax bound, so the installed product is detected and removed in
         EVERY direction — older, same-version rebuild (new ProductCode via
         ProductCode="*"), and newer (the 10005 «A newer version is already
         installed» gate the owner hit three times today is gone). The POC
         workflow clicks ANY dist MSI and it must just install. -->
    <MajorUpgrade AllowDowngrades="yes" />
    <MediaTemplate EmbedCab="yes" />

    <!-- Dumb-extractor properties (see header). -->
    <Property Id="ARPSYSTEMCOMPONENT" Value="1" />
    <Property Id="REINSTALLMODE" Value="amus" />

    <!--
      2026-08-28 (owner request #14): real app icon for the Add/Remove
      Programs entry + the non-advertised desktop shortcut. ARPSYSTEMCOMPONENT
      (above) keeps the entry hidden per the 2026-08-24 owner law — the icon
      is wired so any future un-hiding shows the proper asset, not a blank.
    -->
    <Icon Id="MonitorIco" SourceFile="$(var.AssetsDir)\app-icon.ico" />
    <Property Id="ARPPRODUCTICON" Value="MonitorIco" />

    <!--
      2026-08-31 (owner: «не нравится подход [статичной таблички в Burn] —
      полностью переехать на большой GUI как было ... логотип надо
      перенести»): the WIZARD is branded with the Burservis logo. These
      WixVariables feed every stock WixUI page (banner strip on top of each
      dialog + the big Welcome picture); the two custom dialogs below carry
      an explicit BannerBitmap control referencing WixUI_Bmp_Banner.
      The bitmaps are REGENERATED from the source PNG by gen-ui-bmps.ps1
      (invoked from build-msi.ps1 step 9.5) — never edit them by hand.
    -->
    <WixVariable Id="WixUIBannerBmp" Value="$(var.AssetsDir)\ui-banner.bmp" />
    <WixVariable Id="WixUIDialogBmp" Value="$(var.AssetsDir)\ui-dialog.bmp" />

    <!--
      ICEMDIR: iCem install folder (default below). DetectIcemDefault finds an
      existing C:\Program Files\Halliburton\iCem; when absent, the (skippable)
      InstallDirDlg asks the user and binds the answer to this property.
      2026-08-29 (owner request — «установщик предлагает C:\Program Files\...
      \iCem\ хотя мы переехали»): the two paths are SEPARATE — the monitor
      payload (MONITORROOT, ProgramData, migrated) vs. the AddIn target
      (ICEMDIR\Bin\Modules, the iCem app folder). When ICEMDIR is already
      resolved (iCem present — the normal stand case) the directory dialog is
      USELESS and is SKIPPED; it shows only when iCem was NOT found (rare
      stand). ICEMDIR_FOUND drives that skip (set alongside ICEMDIR by the
      search; the literal-default fallback leaves it empty → dialog shows).
    -->
    <Property Id="ICEMDIR" Secure="yes" Value="C:\Program Files\Halliburton\iCem">
      <DirectorySearch Id="DetectIcemDefault"
                       Path="C:\Program Files\Halliburton\iCem"
                       Depth="0"
                       AssignToProperty="yes" />
    </Property>
    <Property Id="ICEMDIR_FOUND" Secure="yes">
      <DirectorySearch Id="DetectIcemFound"
                       Path="C:\Program Files\Halliburton\iCem"
                       Depth="0"
                       AssignToProperty="yes" />
    </Property>

    <!--
      ICEM_RUNNING=1 while any conflicting process is alive (iCem or the
      installed monitor stack; set by the CheckIcemRunning JScript CA from
      assets\CheckConflicts.js; used by the IcemRunningCheckDlg gate).
    -->
    <Property Id="ICEM_RUNNING" Secure="yes" />

    <!--
      OptionsDlg checkboxes (owner request 2026-08-26). Public + Secure so
      the deferred script CAs can read them in the server phase. Unset by
      default = opt-in (unchecked).
    -->
    <Property Id="CREATEDESKTOPSHORTCUT" Secure="yes" />
    <Property Id="ADDAUTOSTART" Secure="yes" />

    <!--
      Directory layout (2026-08-28 AMENDMENT #2 — ProgramData migration;
      2026-08-31 AMENDMENT «1+2» — flat merge):
        [CommonAppDataFolder]\Halliburton\iCem\DataMonitoring <- monitor payload
                                                        (host/shell/emulator
                                                         FLAT at the root —
                                                         one shared WinUI/.NET
                                                         runtime set, exes stay
                                                         independent processes;
                                                         Data.dat + the
                                                         runtime-created
                                                         config.ini live here)
        [ICEMDIR]\Bin\Modules                                <- the iCem AddIn dll
      TARGETDIR-anchored ICEMDIR is property-rooted: when ICEMDIR carries a
      value (default, AppSearch hit or WixUI_InstallDir answer), MSI resolves
      this element to that full path; Name is only a fallback.
    -->
    <StandardDirectory Id="CommonAppDataFolder">
      <Directory Id="HalliburtonDataDir" Name="Halliburton">
        <Directory Id="IcemDataDir" Name="iCem">
          <Directory Id="MONITORROOT" Name="DataMonitoring">
            <!-- 2026-08-31 (owner decree «пункт 3»): the CLIDIR subfolder is
                 RETIRED — the cli merged INTO the host exe (argv mode:
                 iCemDataMonitor.Host.exe snapshot|get|header). Host + Shell +
                 Emulator are flat siblings at the root (HostProcessLauncher
                 resolution). The standalone EMULATORDIR is RETIRED too
                 (owner decree «1+2»); the emulator's sim registry ships
                 renamed (variable_registry.emulator.json) so the host's
                 production registry keeps the canonical name. -->
          </Directory>
        </Directory>
      </Directory>
    </StandardDirectory>
    <StandardDirectory Id="TARGETDIR">
      <Directory Id="ICEMDIR" Name="iCem">
        <Directory Id="ICEMBIN" Name="Bin">
          <Directory Id="ICEMMODULES" Name="Modules" />
        </Directory>
      </Directory>
    </StandardDirectory>

    <!--
      2026-08-28 (owner request #11/#12): native opt-in elements behind the
      OptionsDlg checkboxes — no script CAs, deterministic, removed at
      uninstall. perMachine scope ⇒ DesktopFolder = the ALL-USERS desktop.
      Both components are keyed by HKCU registry values (the standard WiX
      pattern for non-advertised shortcuts / HKCU autostart values inside a
      per-machine install — written to the INSTALLING user's hive, same
      caveat the script approach had).
    -->
    <StandardDirectory Id="DesktopFolder">
      <Component Id="Cmp.DesktopShortcut" Guid="{7F3C9A64-2E81-4B5D-9C36-A10D54F8B721}"
                 Condition="CREATEDESKTOPSHORTCUT=1">
        <Shortcut Id="DesktopMonitorShortcut"
                  Name="iCem Data Monitor"
                  Description="iCem Data Monitor"
                  Target="[MONITORROOT]iCemDataMonitor.WinUI.exe"
                  WorkingDirectory="MONITORROOT"
                  Icon="MonitorIco" IconIndex="0" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKCU"
                       Key="Software\Burservis\iCemDataMonitor"
                       Name="DesktopShortcut"
                       Type="integer" Value="1" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
    </StandardDirectory>

    <ComponentGroup Id="Setup.Options">
      <ComponentRef Id="Cmp.DesktopShortcut" />
      <!-- Autostart target = the HOST with the autostart flag (NOT the
           emulator: the emulator is an independent app, owner decree
           2026-08-27). Value name iCemDataMonitorHost == AutostartManager +
           the SetAutostart RPC — one key, one truth. -->
      <Component Id="Cmp.AutostartReg" Directory="MONITORROOT" Guid="{4A8E1D52-93B7-4F0C-8E2A-6D41C9B5F308}"
                 Condition="ADDAUTOSTART=1">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKCU"
                       Key="Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run"
                       Name="iCemDataMonitorHost"
                       Type="string"
                       Value="&quot;[MONITORROOT]iCemDataMonitor.Host.exe&quot; --autostart"
                       KeyPath="yes" />
        <!--
          Uninstall-correctness (owner request 2026-08-28): a Task Manager
          "disabled" flag outlives the Run value it refers to. If the MSI only
          removed the Run value, a later reinstall with the checkbox checked
          would write the Run value back while the stale flag kept it silently
          OFF. Clearing the flag at uninstall makes every reinstall start
          clean (the host's own SetEnabled(true) does the same for the RPC path
          — AutostartManager TASK MANAGER LAW).
        -->
        <RemoveRegistryValue Root="HKCU"
                             Key="Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\StartupApproved\Run"
                             Name="iCemDataMonitorHost" />
      </Component>

      <!--
        2026-08-31 (owner decree: «после деинсталяции — надо за собой удалять
        файлы C:\ProgramData\Halliburton\iCem\DataMonitoring»): MSI removes only
        files IT installed; runtime-created data (config.ini, Data.dat, Logs\,
        emule_config.xml, startup.log, WebView2 cache, the pre-1.2.0 iCemEmulator\
        subfolder) would linger forever. The wipe is a DEFERRED JScript CA
        (WipeMonitorRoot in assets\CheckConflicts.js) fed by CustomActionData.

        WHY NOT util:RemoveFolderEx (two proven failures 2026-08-31, logs
        uninstall121/uninstall122): (1) the WixRemoveFoldersEx action runs
        BEFORE CostFinalize, so a Directory-id property is 0x80070057
        «Missing folder property»; (2) even with the path composed early its
        junction guard misfired («Path is a junction; skipping») on a plain
        directory and wiped nothing. A direct FSO delete has no such guards.

        CONDITION LAW: REMOVE="ALL" AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE — a real
        uninstall wipes the folder; a MajorUpgrade (whose old-product
        uninstall sets UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE) keeps config.ini/Data.dat alive
        across the upgrade. The old util:RemoveFolderEx component and the
        MONITORROOTWIPE property are retired.
      -->
    </ComponentGroup>

    <!--
      Conflict gate CAs (owner request 2026-08-26, rewrite after the owner
      hit a silent pass-through with iCem running; SECOND rewrite 2026-09-01
      PM — bug report «проверка конфликтов не обновляется» on 1.4.3).
      The logic lives in a Binary-keyed JScript file (assets\CheckConflicts.js)
      — no attribute escaping. DETECTION LAW (2026-09-01 PM): the substring
      rule «name contains icem» is RETIRED (it false-positived on
      Halliburton.iCem.* service-hosted leftovers — LogUpload/SyncService/Web
      — that the SCM kept resurrecting; the gate could never go clean).
      Processes now conflict by EXACT image name (icem.exe + our host/shell/
      emulator/cli); services conflict when Name/DisplayName starts with
      'icem' AND the service is in a RUNNING state (Stopped services never
      block). CheckIcemRunning REWRITES ICEM_RUNNING on every call — that is
      what makes «Обновить» a real re-check; Return="check" (was "ignore"):
      a dead JScript engine must ABORT the install, not silently open the
      gate (the 2026-08-26 «silent pass-through» class).
      CloseConflictingProcesses ("Закрыть всё") stops conflicting services
      FIRST (StopService; SCM owns their processes), settles 3 s, then
      terminates the exact-name processes — iCem.exe included, explicit
      owner decision 2026-08-26.
      CancelAfterUserConfirm (2026-09-01 PM): fires on CancelDlg/Yes and on
      UserExit — the cancel path applies the SAME close logic, so nothing the
      wizard saw survives its death (the report's «had to kill msiexec» class).
    -->
    <CustomAction Id="CheckIcemRunning"
                  BinaryRef="CheckConflictsJs"
                  JScriptCall="CheckConflicts"
                  Execute="immediate"
                  Return="check" />
    <CustomAction Id="CloseConflictingProcesses"
                  BinaryRef="CheckConflictsJs"
                  JScriptCall="CloseConflicts"
                  Execute="immediate"
                  Return="ignore" />
    <CustomAction Id="CancelAfterUserConfirm"
                  BinaryRef="CheckConflictsJs"
                  JScriptCall="CancelAfterUserConfirm"
                  Execute="immediate"
                  Return="ignore" />

    <!--
      2026-08-31 (owner decree «после деинсталяции — удалять за собой
      файлы»): the full-uninstall wipe of DataMonitoring. Deferred +
      Impersonate="no" (elevated, can delete anything); the JScript reads
      ONLY CustomActionData, so the matching SetProperty below carries the
      same Id and is scheduled right before it. Condition (REMOVE="ALL" AND
      NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE): real uninstall wipes; MajorUpgrade keeps
      config.ini/Data.dat across the upgrade. Return="ignore" — cleanup
      must never roll back an uninstall over a locked file.
    -->
    <CustomAction Id="WipeMonitorRoot"
                  BinaryRef="CheckConflictsJs"
                  JScriptCall="WipeMonitorRoot"
                  Execute="deferred"
                  Impersonate="no"
                  Return="ignore" />
    <SetProperty Id="WipeMonitorRoot"
                 Value="[CommonAppDataFolder]Halliburton\iCem\DataMonitoring"
                 Before="WipeMonitorRoot"
                 Sequence="execute" />

    <!--
      2026-08-28: the script CAs (RunCreateShortcutScript/RunAddAutostart-
      Script) are REMOVED — the OptionsDlg checkboxes now drive NATIVE
      components (Cmp.DesktopShortcut / Cmp.AutostartReg, see the directory
      section). The scripts themselves stay shipped under iCemMonitor\scripts\
      for manual ops use only.
    -->

    <!--
      Sequencing: the iCem process gate runs after AppSearch.
      2026-09-01 PM: the wipe CA moved from Before="RemoveFolders" to
      Before="InstallFinalize" — AFTER RemoveFiles emptied the directory
      table, so no reinstall window can resurrect files under the wipe; the
      chain-gone/parents-survive reasoning is unchanged (condition still
      excludes MajorUpgrade).
      The cancel CA is NOT sequenced here — UserExit fires on SUCCESS too,
      so an After="UserExit" kill-CA would terminate iCem after every good
      install (caught in review). It runs ONLY as a CancelDlg/Yes publish.
    -->
    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <Custom Action="CheckIcemRunning" After="AppSearch" />
      <Custom Action="WipeMonitorRoot" Before="InstallFinalize" Condition='(REMOVE="ALL") AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE' />
    </InstallExecuteSequence>
    <InstallUISequence>
      <Custom Action="CheckIcemRunning" After="AppSearch" />
    </InstallUISequence>

    <!-- 2026-09-01 PM (bug report «проверка конфликтов не обновляется»):
         Cancel wiring on the STOCK CancelDlg. Yes = the operator chose to
         abort: run the same close logic (services first, then processes) so
         nothing the wizard touched outlives it — then the stock EndDialog
         proceeds (Order=1 runs first). No = cancel dismissed: refresh the
         gate property so the dialog behind reflects the CURRENT machine.
         WiX v4: package-level Publish rows must sit inside a UI container. -->
    <UI>
      <Publish Dialog="CancelDlg" Control="Yes" Event="DoAction"
               Value="CancelAfterUserConfirm" Order="1" />
      <Publish Dialog="CancelDlg" Control="No" Event="DoAction"
               Value="CheckIcemRunning" Order="1" />
    </UI>

    <!--
      Close running instances before InstallFiles so the extractor never
      hits "file in use". CloseMessage first, TerminateProcess=1 fallback,
      RebootPrompt=no.
    -->
    <util:CloseApplication Id="CloseHostExe"
                           Target="iCemDataMonitor.Host.exe"
                           CloseMessage="yes"
                           TerminateProcess="1"
                           RebootPrompt="no" />
    <util:CloseApplication Id="CloseShellExe"
                           Target="iCemDataMonitor.WinUI.exe"
                           CloseMessage="yes"
                           TerminateProcess="1"
                           RebootPrompt="no" />
    <!-- 2026-08-31: icemdatamonitor-cli.exe is RETIRED (merged into the host
         exe as argv mode, decree «пункт 3») — this entry stays so upgrades
         from <= 1.3.x still close a running legacy cli before its files are
         removed. -->
    <util:CloseApplication Id="CloseCliExe"
                           Target="icemdatamonitor-cli.exe"
                           CloseMessage="yes"
                           TerminateProcess="1"
                           RebootPrompt="no" />
    <!-- 2026-08-27: the standalone emulator app (was iCemEmule.exe +
         iCemEmule.WinUI.exe — both retired with the merged app). -->
    <util:CloseApplication Id="CloseEmulatorExe"
                           Target="iCemEmulator.exe"
                           CloseMessage="yes"
                           TerminateProcess="1"
                           RebootPrompt="no" />

    <!--
      WixUI_InstallDir: shows the install dir edit page bound to ICEMDIR
      (the AddIn target). MONITORROOT is fixed and never asked.
    -->
    <ui:WixUI Id="WixUI_InstallDir" InstallDirectory="ICEMDIR" />

    <!--
      NO red banner / NO red logo strip on the wizard dialogs (owner
      decision 2026-08-26): the solid Burservis red read as an ERROR
      state, not as branding. Dialogs stay stock-looking; Burservis
      branding lives in the BA window (custom theme) and the exe icon.
    -->

    <!--
      Gate dialog (owner request 2026-08-26, reworked after the owner hit a
      silent pass-through with iCem running): detects iCem AND any already
      installed monitor processes (host/shell/cli/emulator — their files stay
      locked). Two ways out when conflicts are found:
        * "Закрыть всё" — the INSTALLER terminates every conflicting
          process (iCem included, explicit owner decision), re-checks and
          advances when clean;
        * "Обновить" — the operator closes the processes manually, then
          re-runs the check.
      "Далее" is enabled only once the check is clean; "Отмена" aborts.
      The gate shows on EVERY scenario (fresh install, upgrade, repair,
      uninstall) — an upgrade with the old host still running is exactly
      the conflict case the owner called out.
    -->
    <!--
      Bare <UI> (no Id): WiX5 merges these rows into the WixUI_InstallDir
      dialog set referenced above — an Id would clash with the wixlib's
      WixUI symbol (WIX0091). The same applies to the WelcomeDlg publish
      override: Order=4 executes after the stock Order=2/3 publishes.
    -->
    <UI>
      <!--
        2026-08-31 (owner amendments, Welcome/Finish pages, paint-mock
        reviewed) — IMPLEMENTED POST-BUILD, not here: WiX v5 REFUSES authored
        overrides of stock WixUI dialogs (WIX0091 duplicate Dialog/Control —
        proven on the 1.4.1 builds). The stock WelcomeDlg/ExitDialog stay
        as authored; installer\patch-welcome-page.ps1 (step 11.5) rewrites
        their Control-table rows inside the BUILT MSI:
          * WelcomeDlg/Title: full width, single line, top, from the left
            edge (25,15,443x16) — no more 220px wrapping box;
          * WelcomeDlg/Description: lower-left above the buttons
            (25,222,443x30);
          * ExitDialog/Title + Description: same lower-left pattern;
          * bitmap (gen-ui-bmps.ps1): subtitle removed, red rule = logo
            width, lower third kept empty for the text controls.
      -->
      <Dialog Id="IcemRunningCheckDlg" Width="370" Height="270"
              Title="[ProductName] — проверка конфликтов" NoMinimize="yes">
        <Control Id="BannerBitmap" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="370" Height="44"
                 TabSkip="no" Property="WixUI_Bmp_Banner" />
        <Control Id="Title" Type="Text" X="15" Y="6" Width="340" Height="15"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Title}Проверка конфликтов" />
        <Control Id="Description" Type="Text" X="25" Y="52" Width="320" Height="28"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Перед установкой нужно закрыть iCem, службы iCem и компоненты iCem Data Monitor — их файлы будут заняты." />

        <Control Id="RunningText" Type="Text" X="25" Y="94" Width="320" Height="52"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Обнаружены запущенные процессы или службы iCem / iCem Data Monitor. Нажмите «Закрыть всё», и установщик остановит их сам, либо остановите их вручную и нажмите «Обновить»."
                 ShowCondition="ICEM_RUNNING=1" HideCondition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING" />
        <Control Id="OkText" Type="Text" X="25" Y="94" Width="320" Height="28"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Конфликтов не обнаружено — можно продолжать."
                 ShowCondition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING" HideCondition="ICEM_RUNNING=1" />

        <Control Id="Back" Type="PushButton" X="11" Y="243" Width="54" Height="17"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Назад">
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="WelcomeDlg" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="CloseApps" Type="PushButton" X="92" Y="243" Width="72" Height="17"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Закрыть всё"
                 EnableCondition="ICEM_RUNNING=1" DisableCondition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING">
          <Publish Event="DoAction" Value="CloseConflictingProcesses" Order="1" />
          <Publish Event="DoAction" Value="CheckIcemRunning" Order="2" />
          <!-- BUGFIX 2026-08-27 (owner crash, MSI log Error 2856): the OLD
               Order=3 published NewDialog IcemRunningCheckDlg WHILE that same
               dialog was already displayed -> "Creating a second copy of the
               dialog" -> FatalError -> 1603 on every «Закрыть всё»/«Обновить»
               click. A self-refreshing gate must NEVER NewDialog to itself:
               the open dialog re-evaluates its control conditions (texts,
               button enable/disable) as soon as the ICEM_RUNNING property
               changes. Only the CLEAN state navigates forward. -->
          <!-- 2026-08-29: skip the directory dialog when ICEMDIR is already
               resolved (iCem found on the stand) — jump straight to
               OptionsDlg; fall back to InstallDirDlg only when iCem is NOT
               found (ICEMDIR_FOUND empty). See the ICEMDIR property comment. -->
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="OptionsDlg" Order="4" Condition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING AND ICEMDIR_FOUND" />
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="InstallDirDlg" Order="5" Condition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING AND NOT ICEMDIR_FOUND" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Refresh" Type="PushButton" X="169" Y="243" Width="70" Height="17"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Обновить"
                 EnableCondition="ICEM_RUNNING=1" DisableCondition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING">
          <Publish Event="DoAction" Value="CheckIcemRunning" Order="1" />
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="OptionsDlg" Order="3" Condition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING AND ICEMDIR_FOUND" />
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="InstallDirDlg" Order="4" Condition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING AND NOT ICEMDIR_FOUND" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Next" Type="PushButton" X="243" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Далее" Default="yes"
                 EnableCondition="NOT ICEM_RUNNING" DisableCondition="ICEM_RUNNING=1">
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="OptionsDlg" Order="1" Condition="ICEMDIR_FOUND" />
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="InstallDirDlg" Order="2" Condition="NOT ICEMDIR_FOUND" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="303" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17"
                 Cancel="yes" Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Отмена">
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="CancelDlg" />
        </Control>
      </Dialog>

      <!--
        OptionsDlg (owner request 2026-08-26, native since 2026-08-28):
        post-install options as opt-in checkboxes. A checked box turns on the
        matching NATIVE component (Cmp.DesktopShortcut — real <Shortcut> on
        the all-users desktop; Cmp.AutostartReg — HKCU Run value
        iCemDataMonitorHost = "<host exe>" + the autostart flag). Unchecked by
        default.
      -->
      <Dialog Id="OptionsDlg" Width="370" Height="270"
              Title="[ProductName] — параметры установки" NoMinimize="yes">
        <Control Id="BannerBitmap" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="370" Height="44"
                 TabSkip="no" Property="WixUI_Bmp_Banner" />
        <Control Id="Title" Type="Text" X="15" Y="6" Width="340" Height="15"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Title}Дополнительные параметры" />
        <Control Id="Description" Type="Text" X="25" Y="52" Width="320" Height="28"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Выберите, что создать при установке:" />

        <Control Id="DesktopShortcutCheck" Type="CheckBox" X="25" Y="92" Width="300" Height="17"
                 Property="CREATEDESKTOPSHORTCUT" CheckBoxValue="1"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Создать ярлык на рабочем столе" />
        <Control Id="AutostartCheck" Type="CheckBox" X="25" Y="116" Width="300" Height="17"
                 Property="ADDAUTOSTART" CheckBoxValue="1"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Добавить iCem Data Monitor в автозагрузку" />

        <Control Id="Back" Type="PushButton" X="124" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17"
                 Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Назад">
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="InstallDirDlg" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Next" Type="PushButton" X="244" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17"
                 Default="yes" Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Далее">
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="VerifyReadyDlg" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="304" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17"
                 Cancel="yes" Text="{\WixUI_Font_Normal}Отмена">
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="CancelDlg" />
        </Control>
      </Dialog>

      <!-- The gate is UNCONDITIONAL now: fresh install, upgrade, repair and
           uninstall all pass through it (Order=4 executes AFTER the stock
           WixUI publishes, so this navigation wins). -->
      <Publish Dialog="WelcomeDlg" Control="Next" Event="NewDialog"
               Value="IcemRunningCheckDlg" Order="4" />

      <!-- Fresh-install wizard: InstallDirDlg [Далее] -> OptionsDlg
           (checkbox page) before VerifyReadyDlg. Order=5 executes AFTER the
           stock WixUI publishes (Order=1..4: SetTargetPath / validate /
           SpawnDialog InvalidDirDlg / NewDialog VerifyReadyDlg), so on a
           valid path this navigation wins; maintenance flows are untouched. -->
      <Publish Dialog="InstallDirDlg" Control="Next" Event="NewDialog"
               Value="OptionsDlg" Order="5" Condition="NOT Installed" />
    </UI>

    <!--
      Single feature = single uninstallable unit. Payload.All is generated
      by gen-payload.ps1 (ComponentGroupRefs to Payload.Root under
      MONITORROOT and Payload.Addin under ICEMMODULES).
    -->
    <Feature Id="Main" Level="1">
      <ComponentGroupRef Id="Payload.All" />
      <ComponentGroupRef Id="Setup.Options" />
    </Feature>

  </Package>

  <!--
    CheckConflicts.js as an MSI Binary — the JScript source for the
    conflict-gate custom actions (CheckIcemRunning / CloseConflicting-
    Processes). The Burservis dialog branding was removed (owner decision
    2026-08-26: the red fill read as an error state); the logo lives only
    in the BA theme and the exe icon now.
  -->
  <Fragment>
    <Binary Id="CheckConflictsJs" SourceFile="$(var.AssetsDir)\CheckConflicts.js" />
  </Fragment>
</Wix>
